{
  "name": "EventAnnotation",
  "package": "spec",
  "description": "EventAnnotation marks a message as an EventBus event: tacplus generates a topic\n and a publish RPC for it. The producer surface is declared (not defaulted):\n set c2s to expose the publish RPC to external clients (via gateway), s2s to\n expose it to internal services. At least one must be present; an internal-only\n event sets only s2s and is never exposed externally. spec.record implies\n spec.event (a record is an event that is also stored + projectable).",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "c2s",
      "type": "message",
      "description": "c2s, when present, exposes the publish RPC to external clients (via gateway).",
      "message": {
        "name": "MethodC2SAnnotation",
        "package": "spec",
        "description": "MethodC2SAnnotation overrides service-level defaults for a single C2S RPC.\n Only valid on methods within a service_c2s service.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "auth_disabled",
            "type": "bool",
            "description": "auth_disabled: no token required for this RPC.\n Used for public endpoints like OIDC discovery and JWKS."
          },
          {
            "name": "auth_any_user",
            "type": "bool",
            "description": "auth_any_user: any authenticated user can call this RPC\n (no entitlement check). Used for user-facing endpoints where\n any valid token is sufficient (e.g., token exchange, event streams)."
          },
          {
            "name": "target_namespace_field",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "target_namespace_field names the request field whose string value carries\n the target namespace path (e.g. \"/io/example/tenant\"). When set, the C2S\n authorizer enforces the level-or-below rule: the caller's namespace (from\n the bearer token's `namespace` claim) must equal the target namespace or\n be a strict path-segment ancestor of it. The field must exist on the\n request message and be of type string.\n\n Use the proto field name (snake_case as declared), e.g. \"tenant_namespace\".\n Leave unset for RPCs whose target is implicit (e.g. List* methods that\n scope the response to the caller's subtree at the handler).",
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 32768 bytes (default)"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "default_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 32768,
                "defaulted": true,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "default_bound"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "s2s",
      "type": "message",
      "description": "s2s, when present, exposes the publish RPC to internal services.\n Producer surface only; the consumer surface is s2s_subscribe.",
      "message": {
        "name": "MethodS2SAnnotation",
        "package": "spec",
        "description": "MethodS2SAnnotation overrides service-level defaults for a single S2S RPC.\n Only valid on methods within a service_s2s service.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "auth_services",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "auth_services overrides the service-level default for this method.",
            "repeated": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 1024 elements (default)",
              "maximum element size: 32768 bytes (default)"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "default_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1024,
                "defaulted": true,
                "unit": "elements",
                "source": "default_bound"
              },
              {
                "rule": "default_max_element_size",
                "target": "element",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 32768,
                "defaulted": true,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "default_bound"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "auth_disabled",
            "type": "bool",
            "description": "auth_disabled: this RPC handles its own authentication internally.\n The caller interceptor skips this RPC entirely. Used for bootstrap\n bootstrap token-minting RPCs where callers authenticate via\n credentials in the request body (cred pair JWT), not via bearer token."
          },
          {
            "name": "routing_only_services",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "routing_only_services narrows the TYPE a named subscriber's generated\n handler receives. Only meaningful on s2s_subscribe (the consumer half of a\n record/event surface); ignored everywhere else.\n\n Listing a service here GRANTS it nothing. Authorization stays auth_services'\n job alone; this field only narrows what an already-authorized subscriber's\n generated code is typed to see. auth_services keeps its existing meaning\n unchanged, and a subscriber not listed here keeps receiving the full\n message exactly as before (this is additive).\n\n For a listed subscriber, tacplus synthesizes\n\n   message \u003cT\u003eRoutingEnvelope {\n     string delivery_id = 1;  // \u003cT\u003e's (spec.record).key field\n     string recipient   = 2;  // \u003cT\u003e's (spec.store_principal) field\n     string namespace   = 3;  // \u003cT\u003e's (spec.store_namespace) field\n   }\n\n and that subscriber's generated Handler takes \u003cT\u003eRoutingEnvelope instead of\n \u003cT\u003e. Generation FAILS for a type flagged here that declares no\n (spec.store_principal) field (and likewise no (spec.record).key or\n (spec.store_namespace) field, or one of the three that is not a string):\n an envelope with an empty recipient is a routing table nobody can route\n with, so it is refused rather than emitted.\n\n WHAT THIS IS NOT. This is a TYPED boundary, not a memory guarantee. The\n FULL message body still arrives on the wire and is still fully decoded\n inside the subscriber's process; the generated dispatch projects the three\n fields out and drops the decoded message immediately afterwards. The body\n is therefore still reachable from a heap dump, a debugger, or anything that\n logs the decode buffer. What this field delivers is that the subscriber's\n own handler CANNOT be written against the body, because its argument type\n does not have one. Narrowing the wire itself is a separate, broker-side\n change and is not what this field does.",
            "repeated": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 1024 elements (default)",
              "maximum element size: 32768 bytes (default)"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "default_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1024,
                "defaulted": true,
                "unit": "elements",
                "source": "default_bound"
              },
              {
                "rule": "default_max_element_size",
                "target": "element",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 32768,
                "defaulted": true,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "default_bound"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "s2s_subscribe",
      "type": "message (recursive reference: spec.MethodS2SAnnotation)",
      "description": "s2s_subscribe, when present, exposes the SUBSCRIBE RPC of this event's topic\n to the named internal services. See RecordAnnotation.s2s_subscribe for the\n full reasoning; the semantics are identical."
    }
  ]
}

