  "package": "spec",
  "description": "RecordRead declares that this service reads a (spec.record) type's STORED\n ROWS through the record query plane's S2S half.\n\n The USE half of the paired control whose grant half is\n (spec.record).s2s_read. See spec.record_read in the FileOptions block above\n for what it generates and why the transport dependency is implied rather than\n restated.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "record",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "record is the fully-qualified record message name, \"package.Message\"\n (e.g. \"messaging.Message\"). Proto package names are globally unique, so no\n file path is needed; tacplus resolves the name to its declaring file.\n\n A name that resolves to no message, or to a message carrying no\n (spec.record), is a hard generation failure — the same fail-loud posture\n (spec.record).key already takes for a key naming a field that does not\n exist.",
