          "source": "default_bound"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "c2s",
      "type": "message",
      "description": "c2s, when present, asks for a CLIENT-FACING read surface over this record's\n rows, emitted into THIS service's own proto as a synthesized sibling\n service (`\u003cService\u003eRecords`) carrying Get\u003cT\u003e and List\u003cT\u003e.\n\n Absent — which is every declaration that predates this field — the reader\n gets the s2s typed reader and nothing else, byte for byte as before.\n\n The grant half is (spec.record).c2s_read on the record, and it must name\n this service. See the C2SScope comments for what the emitted surface is\n allowed to return.",
      "message": {
        "name": "RecordReadC2S",
        "package": "spec",
        "description": "RecordReadC2S is the USE half of the client-facing read plane: what\n (spec.record_read).c2s asks tacplus to emit.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "scope",
            "type": "enum",
            "description": "scope names which rows the surface may return. See C2SScope.",
            "enum_values": [
              {
                "name": "C2S_SCOPE_PRINCIPAL",
                "number": 1,
                "description": "PRINCIPAL: rows whose owning-principal field equals the caller's subject,\n AND whose namespace equals the caller's tenant. \"My own rows.\"\n\n The principal field is resolved exactly as the egress row filter resolves\n it — (spec.store_principal) on a record field, else (spec.record).owner —\n and ONLY when that field is also an EQ criterion on the generated \u003cT\u003eFilter.\n When it resolves to nothing, generation FAILS rather than degrading to a\n tenant-wide read: on ScottyActivity and AccountingRecord the declared\n `owner` is the PUBLISHING SERVICE, so a filter on it would show a human\n every row in its tenant while looking like it showed them their own."
              },
              {
                "name": "C2S_SCOPE_NAMESPACE",
                "number": 2,
                "description": "NAMESPACE: every row in the caller's tenant, with no principal narrowing.\n A legitimate shape — an org-wide audit feed — but a disclosure decision, so\n it must be written down and can never be what absence means.\n\n DECLARED BUT NOT IMPLEMENTED in v1: generation fails with an explicit\n \"declared but not implemented\" error. The value exists so it cannot be\n invented twice with two meanings."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "exposure",
            "type": "enum",
            "description": "exposure is stamped onto the emitted RPCs' (spec.rpc). INTERNAL (the\n default) keeps the surface inside the cluster boundary; EXTERNAL publishes\n it through the gateway, which is what a mobile or browser client needs.",
            "enum_values": [
